## Discrepancies (classified, with evidence)

1. **uzobctl 0x808 -- suspected spec-vs-RTL divergence (class D,
   ESCALATE).** UM164 existence: `misa.V==1 | mmsc_cfg3.AMM==1`; this
   engine has misa.V=1 (RVV configured), so the spec says EXISTS. The
   probe reports ABSENT, and NEITHER decoder generation (kv_csr_dec.v,
   mk_csr_decode.v) carries an existent term for 0x808. Note UM164 is the
   kv-era SPA revision; the AX6x-era SPA may have moved/dropped the CSR.
   Disposition: transport follows the engine (gate UZOB, off) -- but this
   must be confirmed against the AX66 SPA revision and escalated to the
   spec/RTL owners.
2. **sleepvalue 0x811 -- interpretation-unresolved (class D-lite).**
   UM164 existence: `mmsc_cfg.ESLEEP==1`. Probe: CSR absent; live
   mmsc_cfg drains 0x8070e83340092015 (the ESLEEP bit position needs the
   AX66-era SPA to decode with confidence). No decoder generation
   implements 0x811. Same disposition and escalation as uzobctl.
3. **tcontrol 0x7A5 -- none (spec-legal).** "Trigger Module optional":
   the mk decoder omitting it is legal. The over-claim was OUR
   translation error (class A, fixed: gate TCONTROL, vsim `e23700c`).
4. **mecc_code/mseccfg unconditional -- consistent with the live
   mmsc_cfg.** Present with no ECC RAMs configured and no Smepmp knob;
   the spec conditions key on mmsc_cfg bits the RTL itself drives, and
   the probe's checked read is the arbiter. Class A on our side (gates
   fixed), no spec/RTL disagreement asserted.
5. **mideleg reads 0x1444 at reset -- QEMU model agreement REQUIRED
   (class B, resolved).** With RVH the H-delegation bits (2/6/10/12) are
   read-only-one. QEMU models this only when it instantiates the same
   CPU (`andes-ax66` with `h=on`); with the old ax45mpv family-default
   pairing the oracle false-diffed (`mideleg ref=0x0 got=0x1444`,
   `vlenb ref=0x40 got=0x10`). Fixed driver-side: `{qemu_cpu}` follows
   the engine's qemu-config driver globals, and the `--verify` oracle
   plan carries `hw_engine_id` so it models the same hardware.
6. **QEMU andes-ax66 lacked Smstateen -- class B (QEMU-model gap),
   fixed.** A guest `csrr mstateen0` trapped forever on the fast leg
   (probe: `epc=0x100040 tval=0x30c022f3`). The engine's qemu-config now
   emits `smstateen=on` when RVH/Smstateen is configured (converter
   `f62337b`).
7. **mcache_ctl / mmisc_ctl / mecc_code reset divergence (class B,
   named).** QEMU andes-ax66 resets 0x1800 / 0x48 / 0x0; the mk RTL
   resets 0x5000000100001800 / 0x148 / 0x800000 (RTL-hardwired read-only
   bits). Harmless by construction (write-mask: unwritten CSRs keep the
   engine's own reset), but a stash-compare read-back fixture cannot
   pass -- per-engine `policy_overrides.csv` reclassifies the three as
   verify-only. `--verify` still compares them on written workloads.
8. **d23 (chh_core) macro-naming collateral (class A, fixed).** The
   registration exposed that the macro NAMING axis (plain vs `*_INT`) is
   independent of the decoder FAMILY axis: d23's plain-named CODENSE knob
   was invisible to the kv-only `*_INT` binding (describe-vs-deriver
   parity FAIL). Every generation-varying knob now prefers `*_INT` when
   defined, else the plain name. d23 itself remains UNREGISTERED (its
   `sim_d23` binary is not built here).

